@* 22 Nov 2026 (docs/41, H2): two-step sign-in: set it up with an authenticator app (QR code or key), see and renew recovery codes,
   and turn it off when the role does not require it. Privileged staff are sent here until it is set up (TwoStepRequiredFilter). *@
@model TwoStepViewModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Two-step sign-in";
}

<div class="page-header">
    <div>
        <h1>Two-step sign-in</h1>
        <p>Each time you sign in with your password, GRSMS also asks for a 6-digit code from an app on your phone. A stolen or guessed password alone is then not enough.</p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row g-3">
    <div class="col-lg-7">
        @if (Model.NewRecoveryCodes is { Count: > 0 } codes)
        {
            <div class="card glass mb-3 border border-warning">
                <div class="card-body p-4">
                    <h2 class="h6 mb-2"><i class="fa-solid fa-key text-warning me-1"></i>Your recovery codes: save them now</h2>
                    <p class="small mb-3">If you lose your phone, each code lets you sign in once. Print them or keep them somewhere safe (not on the same phone). They are shown only now.</p>
                    <div class="row row-cols-2 g-2 font-monospace mb-0" aria-label="Recovery codes">
                        @foreach (var c in codes) { <div class="col"><span class="d-block border rounded px-2 py-1 text-center">@c</span></div> }
                    </div>
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary mt-3" data-print><i class="fa-solid fa-print me-1"></i>Print the codes</button>
                </div>
            </div>
        }

        @if (Model.Enabled)
        {
            <div class="card glass mb-3">
                <div class="card-body p-4">
                    <h2 class="h6 mb-2"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check text-success me-1"></i>Two-step sign-in is on</h2>
                    <p class="small mb-3">You have <b>@Model.RecoveryCodesLeft</b> recovery code@(Model.RecoveryCodesLeft == 1 ? "" : "s") left.@(Model.RecoveryCodesLeft <= 3 ? " Make new ones soon." : "")</p>
                    <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2">
                        <form asp-action="RecoveryCodes" method="post">
                            <button type="submit" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary" data-confirm="Make new recovery codes? Your old codes stop working.">Make new recovery codes</button>
                        </form>
                        @if (!Model.Required)
                        {
                            <form asp-action="TurnOffTwoStep" method="post">
                                <button type="submit" class="btn btn-sm btn-link text-danger" data-confirm="Turn off two-step sign-in?">Turn off two-step sign-in</button>
                            </form>
                        }
                    </div>
                    @if (Model.Required)
                    {
                        <p class="small text-body-secondary mt-3 mb-0">Your role must use two-step sign-in. New phone? Ask an administrator to reset it, then set it up again.</p>
                    }
                </div>
            </div>
        }
        else
        {
            @if (Model.MustSetUp)
            {
                <div class="alert alert-warning small"><i class="fa-solid fa-shield-halved me-1"></i>Your role handles staff personal data, so GRSMS asks you to set up two-step sign-in before you continue. It takes about two minutes.</div>
            }
            <div class="card glass mb-3">
                <div class="card-body p-4">
                    <h2 class="h6 mb-3">Set it up</h2>
                    <ol class="small ps-3 mb-3">
                        <li class="mb-2">Install an authenticator app on your phone: <b>Microsoft Authenticator</b> or <b>Google Authenticator</b> (free).</li>
                        <li class="mb-2">In the app, add an account and <b>scan this QR code</b>:
                            <div class="my-2"><img src="@Model.QrDataUri" alt="QR code for GREL GRSMS two-step sign-in" width="180" height="180" class="border rounded bg-white p-1" /></div>
                            Can't scan? Choose "enter a setup key" and type: <code class="user-select-all">@Model.SharedKey</code>
                        </li>
                        <li>Type the 6-digit code the app now shows:</li>
                    </ol>
                    <form asp-action="TwoStep" method="post" class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2 align-items-start">
                        <div asp-validation-summary="ModelOnly" class="alert alert-danger py-2 small w-100 mb-1"></div>
                        <input name="code" class="form-control" style="max-width: 10rem" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="one-time-code" placeholder="123 456" required aria-label="6-digit code" />
                        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Turn on two-step sign-in</button>
                    </form>
                </div>
            </div>
        }
    </div>
    <div class="col-lg-5">
        <div class="card glass">
            <div class="card-body p-4 small">
                <h2 class="h6">Good to know</h2>
                <ul class="mb-0 ps-3">
                    <li>The code changes every 30 seconds; always use the newest one.</li>
                    <li>If codes are refused, check that your phone's date and time are set automatically.</li>
                    <li>Signing in with Microsoft 365 uses Microsoft's own check instead.</li>
                    <li>New or lost phone: use a recovery code, or ask an administrator to reset your two-step sign-in.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
